117
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:59,800
Now, if you know, if you're sitting down watching a television or a performance, you're looking at 30 frames per second.

118
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:17,360
So if it takes 72 hours to transmit one thirtieth of a second, you have to times that 72 hours by 30, and then what you would see would flash on the screen for one second, and you'd have to wait that same amount of time before the next second would flash on the screen.

119
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:19,280
That's where we are with technology.

120
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:40,720
But holography itself is ready to go, and they're doing a lot of very interesting work at MIT, Steve Benton at the Spatial Imaging Group, working with compression techniques, and compression is going to probably be the answer for us, and the internet is really helping us out with that because nowhere is compression needed more than trans transmission of data over our lines.

